  "body": "Stacked on #2964. Review the reentrant punch changes above the parent head `4a94c23ce`.\n\n## What changed\n\nThis PR replaces the convex-only refusal of #2955 with checked reentrant corners. The work is ported onto the zero-step setup writer of #2984 and the measured stock heights of #2964. The old setup writer of this branch is not used.\n\n- `crates/geometry/src/geometry/prism.rs`: `closed_vertical_prism` returns the footprint of a full-height vertical extrusion. The union of the top cap triangles must equal the union of the bottom cap triangles. The cap triangles must not overlap. Each side facet must lie on an oriented boundary face. The mesh must be one closed solid. The function examines each facet, also internal surfaces that slices do not find.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/agie_profile.rs`: the job takes its contour from the verified cap footprint, not from a union of slices. A union of slices can add rounded vertices along a sloping face.\n- `crates/post/src/agie/contour.rs`: a reentrant corner is permitted when the rough offset of the selected stock thickness reaches the nominal vertex within 0.002 mm. The offset comes from `QN2_OFFSETS_UM`.\n- `crates/post/src/agie/spacing.rs` (new): when the contour has a reentrant corner, each profile segment must hold both corner joins. Each pair of nonadjacent segments must keep the swept rough pass apart. The check uses the longest miter plus a full rough offset.\n- The entry stays on a supporting exterior face. The ISO object keeps the nominal vertices. The SBL is the zero-step setup of main, with `ID_PUNCH c_punch` and the 1.0 mm separation.\n- Refusal texts name the native wire EDM job (#3537).\n- `examples/agie/notched-punch.*`: an original 40 × 20 mm punch with a 20 mm wide, 1 mm deep V notch.\n- User guide and `docs/decisions/2956-agie-reentrant-punch.md`.\n- `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`: the Wire Contour row states the checked reentrant support and its limits: the reach check with the rough offset of the selected thickness, the joins on each segment, the spacing of nonadjacent faces and the exterior entry. A notch that fails a check is refused.\n\n## Readings\n\nThese readings are from the offline control on the old branch head `6201b325c`, before the port. That head wrote erosion steps in its own SBL.\n\n- The control plotted all seven faces of the notched punch through the rough cut and three trims.\n- Measured wire offsets were 0.245, 0.155, 0.140 and 0.134 mm.\n- At X0, the four notch tips were at Y 9.246222, 9.155773, 9.140698 and 9.134668 mm. Each value agrees with the nominal slopes and the wire offset.\n- The plot kept the 1 mm separation and returned to the threading hole.\n- The formal check of the control had zero job errors.\n\n### Control check of the ported writer\n\nThe offline control import of `NOTCH20`, `NOTCH40` and `NOTCH80` from the ported writer ran on 2026-11-23: see [the control import comment](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/2968#issuecomment-7115465122). Each work showed `CCB030[0]` after import. After TECCUT, the pass offsets agreed with the row of the selected thickness, and FORMALCHECK reported no errors. The jobs came from stack head `30e6c4c3f`, which contains `1962fd5dc`. The later merges do not change a posted byte.\n\nAfter the port, the notched job has the same SBL as the rectangular `CCSEP20` golden job on the same stock and start hole. Only the ISO object changes.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-post` lib, `agie::reentrant_tests`:\n  - `a_broad_notch_keeps_its_nominal_corner_and_requires_an_exterior_entry`\n  - `a_gentle_but_narrow_notch_cannot_hold_the_rough_corner_joins`\n  - `reentrant_corner_reach_uses_the_rough_offset_of_the_selected_thickness` (a 1.251 mm notch passes at 15 and 20 mm and is refused at 40 and 80 mm)\n  - `the_rough_offset_is_the_largest_resident_offset_at_every_measured_height`\n  - `notched_punch_posts_the_zero_step_setup_and_its_nominal_notch`\n- `camcraft-post` lib, `agie::tests::an_acute_miter_needs_more_stock_than_a_round_corner` (a reentrant notch that opens at 53 degrees is refused)\n- `camcraft-geometry` lib, `geometry::prism::tests` (a cavity, a missing facet and a through opening)\n- `camcraft-app` test `agie_native`, `reentrant::cli_posts_the_notched_punch_from_its_original_mesh` (CLI run, zero working steps, SBL equal to the `CCSEP20` golden file)\n\n## Gate\n\nHead `6443d4f09`. It merges the #2964 head `3a29a5f9d` (with `main` at `44e6a8269`, #3219, and the TECCUT guide fix) into `1962fd5dc`, with no conflict. Then one commit changes the Wire Contour row of `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: batch plan, 1189 steps in 64.7 min, 1 failed, 0 stalled.\n  - The red step is `app suites: rotary_verify`, `a_rough_over_an_oversized_bar_peels_from_the_stock_radius` (2110 against 2064). This is the known red of `main` at `44e6a8269` (#3774, follow-up #3794). This PR does not change rotary code.\n  - Green: `clippy -D warnings`, `post suites: agie_inspection`, `agie_safe_setup`, `script_agie_native`, `app suites: agie_native` (13 passed), `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive` and `example_catalog_edge_work`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-geometry -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Posted bytes: no file under `crates/post/tests/golden/agie-setup/` changed against `1962fd5dc`. `agie_native` compares the notched SBL with the `CCSEP20` golden file and passes.\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree 6443d4f09 origin/main` merges cleanly.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The ported jobs were imported on the offline control (see \"Control check of the ported writer\"). The control is an emulation, not the installed machine.\n- No physical cut was made.\n- No heavy lanes ran (P6).\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: The native wire EDM job files accept a vertical punch with checked reentrant corners and refuse features that the rough wire cannot reach safely.\n\nFixes #2956\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
